<li><span title="raifer.tech"><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://taghistory.raifer.tech/#***/railway/subway_entrance">OSM Tag History</a></span></li>
<li><span title="imagicode.eu"><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://imagicode.eu/map/styleinfo/#style=osmcarto&amp;section=tags&amp;key=railway&amp;value=subway_entrance">StyleInfo</a></span></li></ul></div>
</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>A subway entrance is a place where people enter or exit a subway (metro) station. For example, if a station is underground, this is the surface entrance or exit.
</p><p>It is not the point where you validate your ticket. A subway entrance might get you to underground shops before you reach the platform, or it might get you to an overpass/underpass crossing a street.
</p><p>Mapping subway entrances can be used by pedestrian routing softwares: when exiting a station, it can tell the name of the exit the nearest to your destination (as there is likely no GPS signal to guide you through an underground station).
</p>
